findings.finding:
Insights: Final scores are all 0…2²⁰‑1, each runner gets a unique 20‑bit win‑loss code. At round i, a group of 2ᵐ players (sorted by speed) must split into m winners, m losers; feasible splits are exactly Catalan Cₘ (Dyck words). Recursively, each internal node of the full binary tree (size 2ᵏ) contributes a factor C_{2^{k‑1}}. Thus  

N = ∏_{k=1}^{20} C_{2^{k‑1}}^{2^{20‑k}}  

(where each node of size 2^{k} appears 2^{20‑k} times). Compute ν₁₀(N)=ν₂(N)+ν₅(N). Use νₚ(C_n)=νₚ((2n)!)-νₚ(n!)-νₚ((n+1)!). Sum over all nodes. Finally k = ν₁₀(N) mod 10⁵. Pitfall: ensure Catalan count per node, not per round; handle huge exponents via Legendre’s formula.
